    <title>Digital &amp; Data Sovereignty: Definitions and Technologies for Independence and Resilience</title>
    <link href="https://supramundane.agency/2025/0324-geneva-digital-sovereignty-panel/" />
    <updated>2025-03-24T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <id>https://supramundane.agency/2025/0324-geneva-digital-sovereignty-panel/</id>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.graduateinstitute.ch&quot;&gt;Graduate Institute&lt;/a&gt; hosted
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.graduateinstitute.ch/communications/events/digital-data-sovereignty-definitions-and-technologies-independence-and&quot;&gt;an event&lt;/a&gt;
convened by &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/emrysschoemaker/&quot;&gt;Emrys Schoemaker&lt;/a&gt; to discuss data sovereignty
and infrastructure with the wider UN community. The event opened with a keynote from
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/muhammadoukah/&quot;&gt;Ambassador Kah&lt;/a&gt;, and was followed by a panel
moderated by &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/markscott82/&quot;&gt;Mark Scott&lt;/a&gt; and featuring
interventions from &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/neha-mishra-388a8514/&quot;&gt;Neha Mishra&lt;/a&gt;,
&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/konstantinoskomaitis/&quot;&gt;Konstantinos Komaitis&lt;/a&gt;, and yours
truly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We discussed the rising importance of digital sovereignty in global digital governance, and
more widely in geopolitics and trade.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is part of a series of events on digital sovereignty. Several further ones will be
announced soon and reports are being prepared.&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
